<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-recipient> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The person for whom the manuscript was produced, as distinct from the dedicatee or commissioner. Common in gift manuscripts, royal commissions, and personal correspondence. The recipient is the intended reader or owner of this specific copy."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-notary> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A person with official legal standing who authenticated, witnessed, or recorded the document in a formal legal capacity. Critical for colonial notarial records, manumission documents, legal instruments, and formal attestations in Afro-Atlantic archival contexts. The notarial function is administrative and legal; the notary may not be the scribe or author."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorityType-lineage> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Authority vested in a descent line or transmission chain."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-dedicatee> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ContributorRoleScheme> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorityBasis> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
