<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#basis-appointment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Authority derives from formal appointment by a recognized governing body."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#validFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-authority> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Iroko Historical Society" .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-editor> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A person who prepared the text for transmission or publication, including revisions, additions, corrections, or redactions. Distinguished from compiler (who assembles source material) and from translator (who changes language)."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorityType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Classifies an Authority instance by its structural form."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#jurisdiction-new-spain> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#jurisdictionLabel> "New Spain"@en .
