<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-dedicatee> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The person to whom the work is formally dedicated. The dedication relationship often carries political, patronage, or devotional significance that may illuminate the context of production."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#validFrom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "valid from"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ContributorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A SKOS concept describing the function of a person in the production, transmission, or dissemination of a manuscript, archival object, or text. Covers roles from physical production (scribe, artist) through institutional and financial relationships (patron, commissioner) to textual transformation (translator, compiler, editor). Derived from the vHMML contributor role taxonomy (CC BY 4.0, Hill Museum and Manuscript Library) and extended for Iroko Framework use. Role concepts reside in iroko:ContributorRoleScheme."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-translator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-authority> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#authorityType-council> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#AuthorityType> .
