<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#jurisdictionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "jurisdiction type"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#hasContributorRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Links a person in a specific manuscript or textual production context to their functional role. Range: iroko:ContributorRoleScheme concept. Because the role is context-dependent (the same person may be a patron for one manuscript and a recipient for another), this property is best used within a reification node or named graph associating the person, the role, and the specific object. When used directly on an iroko:ArchivalPerson instance, it asserts a general characterization rather than a context-specific one."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-authority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-framework/> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#role-contrib-attributed> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A person to whom a role is attributed by tradition, later inscription, or scholarly inference, without direct documentation in the manuscript itself. Attribution is a scholarly or community claim — record the basis and asserter of the attribution separately. Distinct from all other roles, which are documented rather than inferred."@en .
